      <div type="clause" n="1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hu">Hu</ref> 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hu_1.lnote.oe.3"/><pb n="192" ed="#liebermann"/>Ærest þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi heo gegaderian á ymb feower wucan, ⁊ wyrce ælc man oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> riht.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="192" ed="#liebermann"/>Inprimis ut conueniant semper ad quatuor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hu_1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> ebdomadas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Hu_1.lnote.oe.4-2"/>, et faciat omnis homo rectum alii.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="193" ed="#liebermann"/>Primum quidem quod semper<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Hu_1.lnote.oe.4"/> circa IIII septimanas congregentur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Hu_1.lnote.oe.5"/>, et quisque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Hu_1.lnote.oe.6"/> alii rectum faciat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="16" ed="#robertson"/>Ærest, þæt hi heo gegaderian á ymb feower wucan, ⁊ wyrce ælc man oðrum riht.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="193" ed="#liebermann"/>Erstens, dass sie [die<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Hu_1.lnote.de.1"/> Eingesessenen des Hundred] sich nach je vier<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_1.lnote.de.2"/> Wochen versammeln<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hu_1.lnote.de.3"/>, und jedermann dem andern [processuale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Hu_1.lnote.de.4"/>] Pflicht erfülle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">First, that they [the inhabitants of the hundred] assemble every four weeks, and that everyone do [legal] right to the other.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="17" ed="#robertson"/>In the first place, they<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Hu_1.robnote.n.1"/> shall assemble without fail every four weeks<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Hu_1.robnote.n.2"/>, and every man shall do justice to his fellow.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="432" ed="#whitelock"/>First, that they are to assemble every four weeks and each man is to do justice to another.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="193"><ref target="clause:IIEw_8">II Ew 8</ref>; <ref target="clause:IEw_Prol">I Ew Pr.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II Ew. 8; I Pr.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_5">III Eg 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="196"><ref target="clause:IIEw_8">II Ew 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="316"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_1-1">III Eg 1.1–4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="316"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_5">III Eg 5–5.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II Ew 8; I [Atr] Pr.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Prolog mit Königsnamen fehlt</hi> [<hi rend="italic">schon Archetyp</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Prologue with the king's name lacking [already in the archetype]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">193</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">193</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-getur <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-getur Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">193</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quisquam <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quisquam Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">tres</hi> <hi rend="italic">später übergeschr. R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">tres</hi> later written above R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">abb'as <hi rend="italic">MHk;</hi> abbates <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">abb'as MHk; abbates Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So Waitz <hi rend="italic">Dt. Verf. Gesch</hi>. I 439. Wenig später steht eine aristokratische Beschränkung der Gerichtsfolge fest; Pol Mai I 544; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Hundred 31</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So Waitz <hi rend="italic">Dt. Verf. Gesch</hi>. I 439. A little later an aristocratic restriction of suit of court is established; Pol Mai I 544; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Hundred 31</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gericht 9. a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gericht 9. a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zitiert durch III Eg 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cited by III Eg 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">131</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Rechtsweigerung 2 ff.; Gerichtsversäumnis 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Rechtsweigerung 2 ff.; Gerichtsversäumnis 2</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Hu_1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the men belonging to the hundred.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Hu_1.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">These provisions give the impression that the hundred was a new thing. This is misleading to a certain extent as the hundred was in existence in the time of Edmund and, in view of III Edm. 2, was already an organised body. The division of the country into hundreds of hides was very much older and is found in the seventh century at least, but there is no evidence for the hundred as a definitely organised unit until the time of Edmund. A monthly public meeting is mentioned in II Edw. 8 which would seem to be the predecessor of the hundred meeting. For a discussion of the relation of the hundred court to the older meeting see Liebermann, <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>. p. 451, <hi rend="italic">s.v. Gericht</hi>, 13–13 <hi rend="italic">n</hi>.</seg></note>
      </div>
